<title>UK: Britain's BBC to air global news programme in U.S.</title>
<headline>Britain's BBC to air global news programme in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's BBC World Service said on Friday it was launching a global news programme aimed at morning commuters driving to work in the United States.</p>
<p>The 50-minute programme, featuring major international news stories, will air on public radio stations across the United States, the BBC said in a statement.</p>
<p>Scheduled to begin on July 1, the broadcast is being produced in association with U.S.-based Public Radio International.</p>
<p>&quot;The United States is an important market and one in which the BBC is determined to have a significant presence,&quot; Sam Younger, managing director of the BBC World Service, said.</p>
